  ["Bahasa Inggris||Explanation||Cause and Effect"]: [
    {"question":"In the sentence 'Because of deforestation, many animal species lose their habitat,' what is the cause?","options":["Deforestation","Many animal species","Losing their habitat","Because of"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The cause is the event that makes the other event happen. Deforestation is what triggers the effect: animal species losing their habitat."},
    {"question":"Which phrase in the sentence 'The event was postponed as a result of the heavy rain' signals the cause-and-effect relationship?","options":["was postponed","as a result of","The event","the heavy rain"],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"'As a result of' is a signal phrase that introduces the cause (heavy rain) and connects it to the effect (the event was postponed)."},
    {"question":"Read the sentence: 'Due to the volcanic eruption, several villages were evacuated.' What is the effect?","options":["The volcanic eruption","Several villages","Several villages were evacuated","Due to"],"correctIndex":2,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The effect is what happens because of the cause. The volcanic eruption (cause) led to the evacuation of several villages (effect)."},
    {"question":"Which signal word below introduces the cause, not the result, in a cause-and-effect sentence?","options":["Therefore","Consequently","Because","Thus"],"correctIndex":2,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"'Because' introduces the reason or cause. 'Therefore,' 'consequently,' and 'thus' introduce the result or effect."},
    {"question":"Which sentence correctly combines the following ideas into a logical cause-and-effect relationship? Idea 1: Illegal logging increases flood risk. Idea 2: Trees absorb and store rainwater.","options":["Illegal logging increases flood risk because trees absorb and store rainwater.","Trees absorb and store rainwater; consequently, illegal logging increases flood risk.","Because trees absorb and store rainwater, illegal logging increases flood risk.","Illegal logging increases flood risk because it removes trees that absorb and store rainwater."],"correctIndex":3,"difficulty":"hard","explanation":"D states the logical relationship: illegal logging removes trees, reducing rainwater absorption, which increases flood risk. A, B, and C reverse the logic by making tree water absorption the cause of floods."},
  ],

